    "created_at": "2023-07-12T09:26:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-12T09:26:32Z",
    "body": "Returning to this dangling thread ... I believe the situation touched on in https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/819 is still handwaved/unresolved here. I think it would be worth to unambiguously work out if `<td>` elements inside the `<thead>` are to be essentially treated as `<th>` elements (and that they should be exposed as such in the accessibility tree) due to the wording in the spec\r\n\r\n> The [thead](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-thead-element) element [represents](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#represents) the [block](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-row-group) of [rows](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-row) that consist of the column labels (headers)\r\n\r\n*or* if there is no such intention of implicitly \"upgrading\" a `<td>` to a `<th>` when it's inside a `<thead>`, in which case the wording in the spec may need to be expanded to provide more nuance.\r\n\r\n/cc @LJWatson @chaals @stevefaulkner",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
