    "created_at": "2023-07-12T17:22:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-12T17:22:20Z",
    "body": "seems like this could be updated to say something like:\r\n>...that consist of the column labels (headers) **and related cells** for the parent [table](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#the-table-element) element,...\r\n\r\nthe first example provided in this section uses `td` elements to provide a description of what the previous row of actual table header represents - so to me that seems an overt example that `td` isn't intended to universally become table headers.",
